## Mandates (the Art Director was constrained by these)

## Color Mandate

This mandate is computed from recent builds and today's signals. Treat it as strong guidance, not law.

- **Target hue range:** 40°–80°
- **Avoid these hue zones (recent palettes):** 16°–76°, 255°–315°
- **Rationale:** Target hue range 40-80° (warm sunny). Recent primary hues: 46°, 285°.

If your chosen primary hue falls outside the target range or inside a forbidden zone, justify why in your color story.

## Shell Mandate

Computed from recent builds. The page shell (footer treatment, brand lockup) and the header (placement, nav treatment, mark size) must be DECLARED choices, not defaults. Treat this as strong guidance, not law.

- **Header placements used recently (avoid):** right-margin, masthead
- **Nav treatments used recently (avoid):** marginal — three lowercase links stacked in the top-right margin of the dark ledger panel, no band, no pills, no border, band — a full-width masthead bar with three uppercase links right-aligned
- **Footer treatments used recently (avoid):** ledger foot — build stamp + season + music folded into the base of the right ledger column, running foot — signals as one line of small caps across the base
- **Brand lockups used recently (avoid):** horizontal-md, masthead-lg
- **Mark size bands used recently (avoid):** 28-44

- **Rationale:** Last 2 shells: 2026-08-30: placement=right-margin, nav=marginal — three lowercase links stacked in the top-right margin of the dark ledger panel, no band, no pills, no border, footer=ledger foot — build stamp + season + music folded into the base of the right ledger column, lockup=horizontal-md (single-color), mark=28-44 | 2026-08-29: placement=masthead, nav=band — a full-width masthead bar with three uppercase links right-aligned, footer=running foot — signals as one line of small caps across the base, lockup=masthead-lg (original), mark=28-44

If today's brief genuinely calls for a recently-used treatment, you may reuse it — justify why in your rationale. Fit > novelty.

## Palette Formula Mandate

Computed from recent builds. The audit that motivated this mandate found 49% of days land on the same "saturated accent on near-black void" FORMULA regardless of hue — hue rotation alone doesn't prevent sameness. Treat this as strong guidance, not law.

- **Ground strategies used recently (avoid):** split-field, dark-field

- **Rationale:** Last 2 declared ground strategies: 2026-08-30: split-field | 2026-08-29: dark-field

Prefer a formula NOT in the recent list (light-ground, dark-void, drench, duotone, split-field). If today's brief genuinely calls for a recently-used formula, you may reuse it — justify why in your rationale. Fit > novelty.

## Hero Source Mandate

Computed from recent builds. The audit that motivated this mandate found 45% of heroes are quote-derived. A quote is a lane, not the default. Treat this as strong guidance, not law.

- **Hero sources:** no back-to-back quote streak to avoid.

- **Rationale:** Last 2 hero sources: 2026-08-30: quote | 2026-08-29: weather

If today's genuinely strongest line is a quote, use it — justify why in your hero rationale. Fit > novelty.

## Composition Mandate

Recency is tracked per axis, not per whole tuple: a value used on any of the last 3 builds is discouraged for that axis. The starting values below are derived from today's date — they are a specific place to begin, not an instruction.

- **columns** — start from `two-equal` (avoid `two-asymmetric`, `single`)
- **axis** — start from `diagonal` (avoid `horizontal`, `vertical`)
- **symmetry** — start from `mirrored` (avoid `left-weighted`, `symmetric`)
- **hero_zone** — start from `full-bleed` (avoid `edge-bound`, `center`)
- **density** — start from `crowded` (avoid `measured`, `sparse`)
- **rhythm** — start from `accelerating` (avoid `syncopated`, `even`)
- **shell_posture** — start from `footer-only` (avoid `marginal`, `standard`)
- **field_ratio** — start from `field-dominant` (avoid `balanced`, `drenched`)

- **Rationale:** Last 2 compositions: 2026-08-30: columns=two-asymmetric axis=horizontal symmetry=left-weighted hero_zone=edge-bound density=measured rhythm=syncopated shell_posture=marginal field_ratio=balanced | 2026-08-29: columns=single axis=vertical symmetry=symmetric hero_zone=center density=sparse rhythm=even shell_posture=standard field_ratio=drenched

Move any axis you have a reason to move, including onto a discouraged value — say why in your rationale, the same as for a recently-used hue. What you must not do is leave all eight sitting on the suggestion because nothing pushed back. Fit beats novelty; sameness beats neither.

Today's starting point reads as: Two columns of matched width, so neither reads as primary and the eye must choose. The primary reading path cuts a corner-to-corner line across the layout. One arrangement repeated in reflection, so the repeat itself is the structure. The hero occupies the entire first screen, edge to edge, with nothing beside it. Deliberate over-packing to the edge of legibility, treated as texture. Intervals shrink as the page descends, so it reads faster toward the bottom. Nothing at the top; all navigation is deferred to the foot of the page. Large areas of color or shape lead, with type placed into them.

## Chassis Mandate

Computed from recent builds. The audit that motivated this mandate found three chassis carrying 71% of all recorded builds while three others had never shipped once. Treat this as strong guidance, not law.

- **Chassis used recently (avoid):** unbounded-figtree, spectral-albert

- **Rationale:** Last 2 chassis: 2026-08-30: unbounded-figtree | 2026-08-29: spectral-albert

If today's hero phrase genuinely demands a recently-used chassis, use it — justify why in your rationale. Fit > novelty.

